{
 "case": "N06-C04-POS",
 "says": "A worker binds their device key and checkout, and a repository knowledge source for Korean tax relief is registered with its applicability (jurisdiction KR, effective from 2026-01-01) and its first revision is committed on the head the registration moved to: a rate table and the prose that explains it. The worker asks which relief applies, naming the condition that changes the answer and pinning that exact revision. The owner keeps the view it answers with privately, moving no head; the view carries the table and the prose cited whole with their digests, the applicability the source states, and evidence naming the pinned revision, with no qualification. A late correction to the table is then committed as a second revision on the head the first moved to; asking the same question pinned to the new revision returns a view whose table member and evidence name the corrected bytes and the second revision. Reopening the first view by its id afterwards returns it unchanged: it still cites the first revision and the original table, so the correction never rewrote an earlier reference.",
